  "auditRules": [
    "A six-category poll row is emitted only when PD, M5S, Lega, FdI and FI/PdL are all explicitly and individually reported. An unreported party is unknown, never zero.",
    "FI and PdL are mapped into one declared research category. This is an editable party-correspondence assumption, not a legal or voter-flow identity.",
    "Other is the complement of the five core categories across mutually exclusive declared party intentions. Do not copy a source row labelled Altri, since remaining named parties also belong here.",
    "Exclude coalition subtotals, previous-wave comparisons, nonresponse, turnout, majority-district coalitions and seat tables. Normalize only the disjoint list/residual support rows.",
    "The SWG 2018 source gives support ranges. This source retains the existing reviewed midpoint estimates and marks denominatorBasis estimated; those ranges are not extra confidence intervals.",
    "All inputs must satisfy publicationDate <= cutoff and fieldworkEnd <= cutoff. Early selections retain their real observation age.",
    "Full sample N is provenance only: the number of decided-voter responses to each party-intention question is unknown.",
    "Historical election results in 2008 do not observe a future FdI category. A model must supply and disclose an editable donor/correspondence rule; no missing poll or historical category is converted silently to zero."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Near-election Camera 2013 has only one admissible six-category poll, SWG pcm-551-q1; the other two terminal questions pool FdI within residual categories.",
    "The four pre-2013 early Demos observations are excluded because they do not individually report FdI. This yields no early six-category poll input for Camera 2013 or the 730-day European 2014 cutoff.",
    "The 13 early Demos observations come from one polling house and all ask about Camera, including those used to predict European targets.",
    "This is a major-party sensitivity input, not a complete municipality-level or coalition-list validation."
  ]
}
